    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0277" n="1111" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 657.119/229</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Norway</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Schmedeman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-12T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 12, 1918—5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>206. Your No. 453, January 9, 2 p.m. Department and War Trade Board will give
                    careful consideration to your suggestions and advise you shortly concerning the
                    publication of our proposal in proper form because we feel that our proposal is
                    fair and reasonable and we think Norwegian people should have full knowledge of
                    our position. For the time being you should defer compliance with Department’s
                    instruction No. 202 of January 5.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
